# 20260811 Claude: the snapshot corpus in transforms/integration-tests/snapshots/ is GENERATED by
# snapshot-regression.py --update, which writes whatever line endings the running OS produces. With
# no rule here the committed snapshots drift into a mix - they were 20 CRLF / 14 LF on 2026-08-11 -
# and every refresh rewrites files by platform rather than by content, so a batch that genuinely
# moved 3 lines can present as a whole-file diff and the real change is invisible inside it. Both
# the CDAFHIR-001 and the seconds/003 batches had to work around this by hand, reading each file's
# existing convention before writing it back. Pinning to LF makes a snapshot diff mean something
# again on every machine, including CI.
#
# Deliberately narrow: ONLY the generated snapshots. The hand-edited sources (.xslt, .xspec, the CDA
# samples under samples/) are left alone - nothing regenerates those wholesale, so normalising them
# would churn a large number of files for no benefit.
transforms/integration-tests/snapshots/*.xml text eol=lf
